# Root build context hardening.
#
# The API Dockerfile (nolsaf/Dockerfile) supports being built from the repository
# ROOT context, where it runs `COPY . .`. Without this file that copy would pull
# the repo root's local secrets and database dumps (.env.local, *.sql,
# remote-backup.sql, backups/) and the entire .git history into the image layers.
#
# The root-context build only ever needs the `nolsaf/` workspace, so default-deny
# everything and re-include just that — then re-exclude secrets and build
# artifacts even inside it, as belt-and-braces.

# 1) Deny everything at the root of the build context.
*

# 2) Re-include only the monorepo the Dockerfile actually builds.
!nolsaf

# 3) Never ship secrets, credentials, or environment files.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# 4) Never ship database dumps or backups.
**/*.sql
**/*.sql.gz
**/backups/

# 5) Never ship VCS metadata or CI config.
.git
.github

# 6) Never ship host build artifacts / dependencies (image runs a clean install).
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

# 7) Never ship logs or local reports.
**/*.log
**/*.err
